---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Wheel and table booking"
	description="Let members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment in one-hour blocks, with booking limits per membership tier and no-show rules."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Wheel time</p>
				<h1>No more racing for the good wheel.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks. You
					decide how many hours each membership tier gets and how far ahead they can book.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Rules per membership tier</h2>
		<p>
			A Basic member might get 8 wheel hours a week, booked up to 3 days ahead. An Unlimited member
			might book up to 7 days ahead with no weekly cap. Set peak hours (evenings and weekends) to
			count double if your studio is always full after 5pm.
		</p>

		<h2>Equipment, not just wheels</h2>
		<p>
			Add anything members share: a slab roller, an extruder, the spray booth, the good banding
			wheel. Each one gets its own calendar and its own rules.
		</p>

		<h2>Cancellations and no-shows</h2>
		<p>
			Set a cancellation window (48 hours is common) and decide what a no-show costs: a lost hour, a
			fee, or a warning on the first one. Freed-up slots appear on the calendar right away.
		</p>

		<h2>Open studio check-in</h2>
		<p>
			Put a tablet by the door. Members tap their name when they arrive, and you always know who is
			in the building, which matters when the kilns are running.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
